       These  routines  return  the  integer  EERRRR upon failure and an OOKK (SVr4
       specifies only “an integer value other than EERRRR”) upon successful  com‐
       pletion.

       X/Open  defines  no error conditions.  In this implementation, ccooppyywwiinn,
       oovveerrllaayy and oovveerrwwrriittee return an error if either of the window  pointers
       are null, or if some part of the window would be placed off-screen.

